<title>RUSSIA: Russian 3-mth T-bill yield falls to 54.69 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 3-mth T-bill yield falls to 54.69 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on a new tranche of three-month GKO Treasury bills fell to 54.69 percent at an auction on Wednesday from 69.12 percent at the last auction of three-month paper on September 25, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The T-bill yielded an average 65.77 percent when it was first issued on September 4.</p>
<p>Full details of the issue follow:  </p>
<p>				     Oct 2		Sept 25</p>
<p>    Series number		21070		21071</p>
<p>    Issue volume		 1.50 trln rbls   4.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		1.00 million	   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	     3.71 trln	  7.90 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	     1.49 trln	  3.91 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		     1.31 trln	  3.19 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	     87.77 pct	  81.61 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	     54.69 pct	  69.12 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price   87.52 pct	  81.51 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield  55.97 pct	  69.58 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)	  93 days	    119 days</p>
<p>    Issue date		   Oct 2, 1996	Sept 25, 1996</p>
<p>    Maturity date		Jan 3,1997	 Jan 22, 1997</p>
<p>On October 2 the finance ministry is also offering 8.50 trillion roubles in a new issue of six-month T-bills (22052) and repaying about six trillion roubles in a maturing issue of six-month T-bills (22027).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
